Sanity in Lovecraftian terms is more a measure of how much of a player's
mind is left.  As any character's knowledge of the Cthulhu Mythos
increases, (ie. the character learns more and more about how much humans
are a small 'bug on the windshield' compared to the rest of the
universe, and how horrific that universe can be...) that same
character's maximum Sanity decreases, which accounts for the behavior of
those loons who run 'round declaring that aliens have spoken to them.

It's not a measure of the player's risk-taking willingness, but in fact
of their actual sanity.

